IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), s 5: insurable employment. Written by the keel agent (ei-g0).
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Seat: a person asking whether their work counts as insurable employment.
--
-- The statute decides most of this from facts the person can state. Three things it hands elsewhere:
--   - what the Regulations include or exclude under s 5(4), (5) and (6): regs 2 to 6 include, regs 7 and 8
--     exclude (piece er1); here each is one BOOLEAN, `included by regulations ...` / `excluded by regulations ...`;
--   - whether persons deal with each other at arm's length: the Income Tax Act decides (s 5(3)(a)), and the
--     Minister of National Revenue's satisfaction decides the exception in s 5(3)(b); each is one BOOLEAN;
--   - what "casual nature" means: s 5(7) lets regulations define it and the Regulations in this folder do not,
--     so it is a plain BOOLEAN.
-- The "whether ... or ..." clauses of s 5(1)(a) (written or oral, who pays, by time or by the piece) are not
-- conditions: they say what does not matter, so they have no input.

§ `Section 5(1) - types of insurable employment`

-- src:91 | (a) employment in Canada by one or more employers, under any express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship, written or oral, whether the earnings of the employed person are received from the employer or some other person and whether the earnings are calculated by time or by the piece, or partly by time and partly by the piece, or otherwise;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1)(a) (src:91)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by one or more employers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1)(a) employment under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `by one or more employers`
    AND `under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship`

-- src:92 | (b) employment in Canada as described in paragraph (a) by Her Majesty in right of Canada;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1)(b) (src:92)
GIVEN `employment as described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1)(b) employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada` IF
        `employment as described in paragraph (a)`
    AND `by Her Majesty in right of Canada`

-- src:93 | (c) service in the Canadian Forces or in a police force;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1)(c) (src:93)
GIVEN `service in the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `service in a police force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1)(c) service in the Canadian Forces or in a police force` IF
       `service in the Canadian Forces`
    OR `service in a police force`

-- src:94 | (d) employment included by regulations made under subsection (4) or (5); and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1)(d) (src:94)
GIVEN `employment included by regulations made under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1)(d) employment included by regulations` IF
    `employment included by regulations made under subsection (4) or (5)`

-- src:95 | (e) employment in Canada of an individual as the sponsor or co-ordinator of an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1)(e) (src:95)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `of an individual as the sponsor or co-ordinator of an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1)(e) employment as the sponsor or co-ordinator of an employment support measure` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `of an individual as the sponsor or co-ordinator of an employment support measure`
    AND NOT (`the measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)`)

-- src:90 | 5 (1) Subject to subsection (2), insurable employment is
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1) (src:90)
GIVEN `paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) insurable employment, before subsection (2)` IF
       `paragraph (a)`
    OR `paragraph (b)`
    OR `paragraph (c)`
    OR `paragraph (d)`
    OR `paragraph (e)`

§ `Section 5(2) and (3) - excluded employment`

-- (c), (d) and (e) are the three exclusions the Regulations may displace: s 5(4)(d), (e) and (f) let
-- regulations include provincial, foreign-government and international-organization employment, and regs 2
-- and 3 say they do so "except for" those paragraphs. So each takes one more BOOLEAN. Assumed, not
-- ruled: that is how s 5(1), which is "Subject to subsection (2)", fits with s 5(4)(d) to (f); see NOTES.md.

-- src:98 | (a) employment of a casual nature other than for the purpose of the employer’s trade or business;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(a) (src:98)
GIVEN `employment of a casual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of the employer's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(a) employment of a casual nature other than for the purpose of the employer's trade or business` IF
        `employment of a casual nature`
    AND NOT (`for the purpose of the employer's trade or business`)

-- src:99 | (b) the employment of a person by a corporation if the person controls more than 40% of the voting shares of the corporation;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(b) (src:99)
GIVEN `the employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the person controls` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(b) employment of a person by a corporation they control` IF
        `the employer is a corporation`
    AND `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the person controls` GREATER THAN 40%

-- src:100 | (c) employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(c) (src:100)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by Her Majesty in right of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(c) employment by Her Majesty in right of a province` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `by Her Majesty in right of a province`
    AND NOT (`included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(d)`)

-- src:101 | (d) employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada or of any political subdivision of the other country;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(d) (src:101)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the government of a country other than Canada or of any political subdivision of the other country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(d) employment by a foreign government` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `by the government of a country other than Canada or of any political subdivision of the other country`
    AND NOT (`included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(e)`)

-- src:102 | (e) employment in Canada by an international organization;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(e) (src:102)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(e) employment by an international organization` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `by an international organization`
    AND NOT (`included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(f)`)

-- src:103 | (f) employment in Canada under an exchange program if the employment is not remunerated by an employer that is resident in Canada;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(f) (src:103)
GIVEN `employment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under an exchange program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `remunerated by an employer that is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(f) employment under an exchange program` IF
        `employment in Canada`
    AND `under an exchange program`
    AND NOT (`remunerated by an employer that is resident in Canada`)

-- src:104 | (g) employment that constitutes an exchange of work or services;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(g) (src:104)
GIVEN `employment that constitutes an exchange of work or services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(g) employment that constitutes an exchange of work or services` IF
    `employment that constitutes an exchange of work or services`

-- src:105 | (h) employment excluded by regulations made under subsection (6); and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(h) (src:105)
GIVEN `employment excluded by regulations made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(h) employment excluded by regulations` IF
    `employment excluded by regulations made under subsection (6)`

-- s 5(3)(a): the Income Tax Act decides whether persons deal at arm's length, so that answer is an input.
-- s 5(3)(b): where the employer is related to the employee within the meaning of that Act, they are DEEMED
-- to deal at arm's length if the Minister of National Revenue is satisfied of what (b) describes. The
-- satisfaction is the Minister's, so it is an input and never worked out here: with it the employment
-- is not excluded, without it the related persons are not at arm's length.
-- src:106 | (i) employment if the employer and employee are not dealing with each other at arm’s length.
-- src:108 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(i),
-- src:109 | (a) the question of whether persons are not dealing with each other at arm’s length shall be determined in accordance with the Income Tax Act; and
-- src:110 | (b) if the employer is, within the meaning of that Act, related to the employee, they are deemed to deal with each other at arm’s length if the Minister of National Revenue is satisfied that, having regard to all the circumstances of the employment, including the remuneration paid, the terms and conditions, the duration and the nature and importance of the work performed, it is reasonable to conclude that they would have entered into a substantially similar contract of employment if they had been dealing with each other at arm’s length.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2)(i), s 5(3) (src:106) (src:108-110)
GIVEN `the persons are not dealing with each other at arm's length, as determined in accordance with the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is related to the employee within the meaning of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of National Revenue is satisfied that it is reasonable to conclude that they would have entered into a substantially similar contract of employment if they had been dealing with each other at arm's length` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2)(i) employment if the employer and employee are not dealing with each other at arm's length` IF
        `the persons are not dealing with each other at arm's length, as determined in accordance with the Income Tax Act`
    AND NOT (`the employer is related to the employee within the meaning of the Income Tax Act` AND `the Minister of National Revenue is satisfied that it is reasonable to conclude that they would have entered into a substantially similar contract of employment if they had been dealing with each other at arm's length`)

-- src:97 | (2) Insurable employment does not include
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(2) (src:97)
GIVEN `paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2) insurable employment does not include` IF
       `paragraph (a)`
    OR `paragraph (b)`
    OR `paragraph (c)`
    OR `paragraph (d)`
    OR `paragraph (e)`
    OR `paragraph (f)`
    OR `paragraph (g)`
    OR `paragraph (h)`
    OR `paragraph (i)`

§ `Section 5 - insurable employment`

-- src:90 | 5 (1) Subject to subsection (2), insurable employment is
-- src:97 | (2) Insurable employment does not include
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 5(1), s 5(2) (src:90) (src:97)
GIVEN `it is insurable employment under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is employment that subsection (2) says insurable employment does not include` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 insurable employment` IF
        `it is insurable employment under subsection (1)`
    AND NOT (`it is employment that subsection (2) says insurable employment does not include`)
